  "answer_text": "It looks like the NBA is currently in the **2026 NBA Finals**, with the New York Knicks facing the San Antonio Spurs! Here's where and how you can get tickets:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc0 Current NBA Action: 2026 NBA Finals\nThe Knicks currently hold a 2-0 series lead against the Spurs after Game 2 of the 2026 NBA Finals. Upcoming games are still available!\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf9f\ufe0f Where to Buy Tickets\n\n1. **Ticketmaster** *(Official NBA Ticketing Partner)*\n   - NBA tickets for the 2025-2026 season are available on Ticketmaster, the **Official Ticketing Partner of the NBA**.\n   - Visit: [ticketmaster.com/nba](https://www.ticketmaster.com/nba)\n   - If tickets for a game are sold out, additional seats may become available closer to the game, so keep checking back.\n\n2. **NBA.com**\n   - You can check the full schedule and find ticket links directly at [nba.com/schedule](https://www.nba.com/schedule).\n\n3. **AmericanArenas.com**\n   - NBA Finals tickets for 2026 start at **$1,009**. You can compare ticket prices and explore upcoming games through the season.\n\n4. **NBATickets.us**\n   - Offers NBA tickets and VIP packages for current and upcoming games, with average ticket prices ranging from **$30 to $200** for the regular season.\n\n5. **ESPN**\n   - The complete NBA season schedule on ESPN includes game times, TV listings, and ticket information for all NBA games.\n   - Visit: [espn.com/nba/schedule](https://www.espn.com/nba/schedule)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips\n- Ticket prices depend on factors like date, time, city, matchup, and seat location. The average ticket for a regular-season NBA game can cost anywhere between **$100\u2013$200**.\n- Plan to arrive at least an hour before tip-off to allow time to park, get through security, find your seats, and catch the pre-game warm-ups.\n\nWould you like help finding tickets for a specific team or game?",
